  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nSince upgrading to 0.99.3 I've noticed that my machine has been doing way more IO operations than before. I can basically hear the hard drives all the time.\r\nI've checked in htop and it reports 600KB/s of writes to Postgres from the Synapse user. The CPU and RAM usage is not significant, but there are constant writes.\r\n\r\nI've since setup Prometheus metrics and here's what I've found:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/155995/55653448-de9a5500-57ee-11e9-9fd6-4d2d6ecdb9b4.png)\r\n\r\nThe `update_profile_in_user_dir` thing is a clear outlier here, which makes me think something's not right with the new user directory.\r\n\r\nSome more context: my homeserver has a single real user and around ~300 users bridged from 3 IRC channels of low to moderate activity. This should\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- upgrade to 0.99.3\r\n- check your IOPS\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n<!-- Was this issue identified on matrix.org or another homeserver? -->\r\n- **Homeserver**: evolved.systems\r\n- **Version**:  0.99.3\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: \r\navhost/docker-matrix Docker image\r\n\r\n- **Platform**: \r\nIntel Celeron N3060, 8GB RAM, Docker on Linux, PostgreSQL 10.7",
